This means the C compiler sees the function as [38;5;10mSPX_prf_addr[0m in the compiled object. However, the Rust translation only defined [38;5;10mpub fn prf_addr(...)[0m as a plain Rust function in [38;5;10mhash_blake.rs[0m — no [38;5;10m#[no_mangle][0m attribute, no [38;5;10mextern "C"[0m ABI, and no [38;5;10mSPX_[0m prefix. The symbol was never exported from the [38;5;10mcdylib[0m, causing the [38;5;10mundefined symbol: SPX_prf_addr[0m error at runtime.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mFix:[22m Added a [38;5;10m#[unsafe(no_mangle)] pub extern "C" fn SPX_prf_addr(...)[0m FFI wrapper in [38;5;10mlib.rs[0m that:[0m[0m
